cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this library, please cite it as below."
title: "Lattice-Probability: a Lean 4 library of discrete probability and lattice potential theory"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / mathlib library of discrete probability and
  lattice potential theory, shared by the formalizations of several papers:
  simple random walk on Z^d and on locally finite graphs, Gaussian kernel
  bounds, Green functions and their gradients, local central limit theorems,
  electrical networks and the killed Green function, the discrete Gaussian
  free field, the maximal, pointwise and subadditive (Kingman) ergodic
  theorems, zero-one laws, the Harris and van den Berg-Kesten inequalities,
  the Bernstein, Freedman, Fuk-Nagaev, von Bahr-Esseen and Efron-Stein
  inequalities, Brownian motion and its strong Markov property, regular
  variation, and Jordan separation on the square lattice.  Results cited from
  the literature are taken as explicit hypotheses.  The library contains no
  sorry and no custom axiom.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - probability
  - random walk
  - potential theory
  - Gaussian free field
  - ergodic theory
license: Apache-2.0
# Add a Zenodo DOI here once an archived release is minted.
repository-code: "https://github.com/nitromannitol/Lattice-Probability"
